# E1 slide routing (TRD §13.1). One JSON object per line; eighteen items, three per category.
#
# `expected_slide` is where the deck must end up; null means it must not move.
# `expected_source` records how the move is expected to happen: "llm" when the model should call
# go_to_slide, "fallback" when the server's alias scoring is the safety net, "none" when nothing
# should navigate. Accuracy is measured on `expected_slide`; `expected_source` informs E6 only.
#
# Sized to the free tier (EVALS.md, 2026-09-11): a navigating item is two model calls of about
# 2,800 tokens against a daily bucket of 200,000, so eighteen items are roughly thirty calls and
# under half a day. The forty-item set this replaced was a full day on its own.
#
# Deck: 1 Anatomy of a Voice Agent / 2 The Latency Budget / 3 Hearing: VAD and Turn-Taking /
# 4 Barge-in: Interrupting Gracefully / 5 Thinking: Tool Calling and Intent Routing /
# 6 Trade-offs and What's Next
